endpoint=gateway:wallet-add-fund on BOTH the transport and the HTTP callback.
NOT /payment-mobile.

Falsifier + could the instrument produce it?  YES: /payment-mobile is a live
value of the same enum and the unit run below actually emits that exact string,
so a mislabelled wallet failure would have been visible. It did not occur.

## order + subscription labels: unit seam only, NOT field-demonstrated
The order label needs a real Place Order (a DB write) -- forbidden by the
read-only rule. Covered by the gate test:
  00:00 +5: endpoint label per entry point each entry point logs its OWN label, and only order is a real route
  [FAIL] endpoint=/payment-mobile http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="payment_webview_load_failed"
  [FAIL] endpoint=gateway:wallet-add-fund http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="payment_webview_load_failed"
  [FAIL] endpoint=gateway:subscription http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="payment_webview_load_failed"
  00:00 +6: endpoint label per entry point the wallet and subscription labels are distinct, constant, and query-free

## Note on the ticket's framing
The brief says the old code 'hardcoded one label for every flow'. Measured:
the old code logged NO endpoint at all -- AppLogger.warn(String) has no
endpoint parameter. The fix therefore ADDS the label dimension rather than
correcting a wrong one.

## Unrelated [FAIL] lines in the same captures
